%I A402173 #13 Nov 22 2026 19:16:41
%S A402173 1,2,4,10,29,144,752,4390,26370,170450,1143970,7971541,57285681,
%T A402173 422219407,3180996434
%N A402173 Number of primes p < 10^n such that p+2, 2p+1, 2p+3 are also primes.
%H A402173 Henri Lifchitz, <a href="http://www.primenumbers.net/Henri/us/NouvChPus.htm">New chains of prime numbers</a>.
%H A402173 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bi-twin_chain">Bi-twin chain</a>.
%F A402173 The Hardy-Littlewood conjecture, generalized to linear forms--which is also covered by the Bateman-Horn conjecture--predicts a correction constant of 4.151180863; therefore, a(n) will be close to 4.15118*10^n/(log(10^n)^4).
%e A402173 {5, 7, 11, 13} and {29, 31, 59, 61} and {659, 661, 1319, 1321} and {809, 811, 1619, 1621} are < 10^3, so a(3) = 4.
%t A402173 Table[Length[Select[Prime /@ Range[PrimePi[10^n]], PrimeQ[# + 2] && PrimeQ[2 # + 1] && PrimeQ[2 # + 3] &]], {n, 1, 7}]
%o A402173 (PARI) vector(7, m, #select(p -> isprime(p+2)&&isprime(2*p+1)&&isprime(2*p+3), primes([2, 10^m])))
%Y A402173 Cf. A066388.
%K A402173 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A402173 1,2
%A A402173 _Henri Lifchitz_, Nov 14 2026
